{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44246156",
      "title": "Changing Server to Client Components",
      "sourceHash": "63dc23317f1a1980bc4f8f4b9ae16778da0de0703d9052bef51e6ae1bf4baaf8",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 5.01,
          "en": "So how can we now change this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.01,
          "end": 8.7,
          "en": "from a server component to a client component?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.7,
          "end": 13.29,
          "en": "Well, by adding a special directive at the top of the file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.29,
          "end": 16.26,
          "en": "and this directive is simply a string with opening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.26,
          "end": 17.49,
          "en": "and closing quotes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.49,
          "end": 21.81,
          "en": "where between the quotes you type use client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.81,
          "end": 24.87,
          "en": "And it doesn't matter if it's double or single quotes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.87,
          "end": 27.003,
          "en": "and you also don't need the semicolon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.99,
          "end": 31.26,
          "en": "This directive, when added at the top of the file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.26,
          "end": 34.83,
          "en": "will tell the project setup, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.83,
          "end": 36.72,
          "en": "that this code, this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.72,
          "end": 38.94,
          "en": "should be treated differently,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.94,
          "end": 41.4,
          "en": "that it should not be executed on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.4,
          "end": 44.1,
          "en": "but that instead here we have some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.1,
          "end": 45.75,
          "en": "that should be sent to the client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.75,
          "end": 48.093,
          "en": "and that should be executed on the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.08,
          "end": 52.02,
          "en": "And actually this wasn't even entirely correct,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.02,
          "end": 54.78,
          "en": "this will still be executed on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.78,
          "end": 56.16,
          "en": "but not just there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.16,
          "end": 59.193,
          "en": "it will also be executed on the client instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.18,
          "end": 64.35,
          "en": "So therefore, with this change made, if you now reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.35,
          "end": 67.11,
          "en": "you see ClientDemo being rendered here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.11,
          "end": 70.32,
          "en": "and it's rendered twice due to strict mode",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.32,
          "end": 72.63,
          "en": "in this demo project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.63,
          "end": 75.15,
          "en": "But you see that being rendered here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.15,
          "end": 79.92,
          "en": "and you also still see it here on the server side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.92,
          "end": 84.15,
          "en": "because again, it is rendered there and on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.15,
          "end": 87.27,
          "en": "So that's how client components work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.27,
          "end": 88.53,
          "en": "But the question of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.53,
          "end": 93.24000000000001,
          "en": "is why would you convert a component to a client component?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.24000000000001,
          "end": 97.32,
          "en": "Why would you not leave it as a server component?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.32,
          "end": 100.89,
          "en": "So what's the advantage of having a client component?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.89,
          "end": 103.38,
          "en": "Well, first let's take a look at the advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.38,
          "end": 104.82,
          "en": "of having a server component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.82,
          "end": 107.49000000000001,
          "en": "And here are the advantage is that of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.49000000000001,
          "end": 110.97,
          "en": "less code has to be sent to the client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.97,
          "end": 112.86,
          "en": "because it's rendered on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.86,
          "end": 115.38,
          "en": "hence, the client doesn't need to download",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.38,
          "end": 119.43,
          "en": "all the code that's required to render this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.43,
          "end": 123.66,
          "en": "So that can improve the performance of our web application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.66,
          "end": 125.79,
          "en": "In addition, as you will see later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.79,
          "end": 128.58,
          "en": "we can even fetch data on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 128.58,
          "end": 129.81,
          "en": "and therefore make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 129.81,
          "end": 131.91,
          "en": "that this doesn't happen on the client side,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.91,
          "end": 134.46,
          "en": "which allows us to send finished pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.46,
          "end": 138.12,
          "en": "that even include data that has to be fetched to the client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 138.12,
          "end": 139.53,
          "en": "on the initial request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.53,
          "end": 142.95,
          "en": "instead of performing data fetching in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 142.95,
          "end": 146.19,
          "en": "which adds an extra delay between the page load",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 146.19,
          "end": 148.11,
          "en": "and when the data arrives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 148.11,
          "end": 149.82,
          "en": "So that's another advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 149.82,
          "end": 152.973,
          "en": "we'll see a little bit later in this section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 153.87,
          "end": 156.57,
          "en": "But why would you then convert a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 156.57,
          "end": 158.88,
          "en": "to a client component?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 158.88,
          "end": 162.87,
          "en": "Well, the answer is relatively straightforward",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 162.87,
          "end": 167.87,
          "en": "because you might need to use some client component feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.66,
          "end": 170.55,
          "en": "in your component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 170.55,
          "end": 173.73,
          "en": "Like for example, the useState() hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 173.73,
          "end": 178.14,
          "en": "If you need to manage state in one of your components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.14,
          "end": 180.243,
          "en": "let's say a counter state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.22,
          "end": 184.8,
          "en": "then you need to convert this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.8,
          "end": 186.06,
          "en": "to a client component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 186.06,
          "end": 190.86,
          "en": "because state can only be managed in client components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.86,
          "end": 195.36,
          "en": "And most React hooks can only be used in client components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 195.36,
          "end": 197.01,
          "en": "Like for example, context,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.01,
          "end": 200.013,
          "en": "would be another client component feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 200.91,
          "end": 205.5,
          "en": "So if you, let's say, have a button in your component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.5,
          "end": 208.653,
          "en": "which is used to increase this counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 209.76,
          "end": 211.95,
          "en": "So in there you call setCount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 211.95,
          "end": 214.8,
          "en": "and you update the count based on the previous count",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 214.8,
          "end": 216.873,
          "en": "as you learned earlier in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 217.95,
          "end": 219.93,
          "en": "And if you then maybe also have a span",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 219.93,
          "end": 222.12,
          "en": "where the count is output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 222.12,
          "end": 223.98,
          "en": "If you have code like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 223.98,
          "end": 227.01,
          "en": "and most importantly if you are managing state, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 227.01,
          "end": 230.883,
          "en": "then you must mark this component as a client component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 232.17000000000002,
          "end": 234.57,
          "en": "And then with that you have this working button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 236.04,
          "end": 239.55,
          "en": "So that would be a reason for a converting a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 239.55,
          "end": 241.98,
          "en": "to a client component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 241.98,
          "end": 244.65,
          "en": "Now here, I'll remove this code again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 244.65,
          "end": 246.63,
          "en": "but I'll leave the state in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 246.63,
          "end": 250.413,
          "en": "so that it's very clear why we need a client component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 252.21,
          "end": 255.54,
          "en": "So that's why we have two kinds of components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 255.54,
          "end": 259.77,
          "en": "in modern React if you are in a project that supports it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 259.77,
          "end": 263.34,
          "en": "We have server components which never execute on the client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 263.34,
          "end": 266.55,
          "en": "but which therefore return the finished page to the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 266.55,
          "end": 269.494,
          "en": "And where you can fetch data and use async await",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 269.494,
          "end": 271.77,
          "en": "as you will see later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 271.77,
          "end": 274.676,
          "en": "and these components are entirely rendered on the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 274.676,
          "end": 278.82,
          "en": "and the finished HTML code is then sent back to the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 278.82,
          "end": 282.69,
          "en": "But as mentioned, a special project setup is required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 282.69,
          "end": 284.103,
          "en": "in order to have them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 284.94,
          "end": 286.62,
          "en": "Client components on the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 286.62,
          "end": 289.86,
          "en": "are executed on the server and the client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 289.86,
          "end": 291.9,
          "en": "so they can run on the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 291.9,
          "end": 295.17,
          "en": "And therefore, client side features like useState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 295.17,
          "end": 296.103,
          "en": "can be used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 297.06,
          "end": 299.79,
          "en": "Now most React projects, like for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 299.79,
          "end": 303.87,
          "en": "projects created with Vite only support client components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 303.87,
          "end": 306.72,
          "en": "at least at the point of time where I'm recording this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 306.72,
          "end": 308.85,
          "en": "So you need a special project set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 308.85,
          "end": 310.92,
          "en": "that supports server components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 310.92,
          "end": 312.93,
          "en": "Client components on the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 312.93,
          "end": 316.08,
          "en": "are the kind of component you've always worked with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 316.08,
          "end": 317.49,
          "en": "over all these years",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 317.49,
          "end": 319.89,
          "en": "because they are the default component type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 319.89,
          "end": 322.59,
          "en": "in most React projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 322.59,
          "end": 326.73,
          "en": "Now, if a project does support React server components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 326.73,
          "end": 330.09,
          "en": "then client components are not the default anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 330.09,
          "end": 334.05,
          "en": "And instead to convert a component to a client component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 334.05,
          "end": 338.82,
          "en": "you have to market as such with the use client directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 338.82,
          "end": 342.48,
          "en": "That's what you should know about React server components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 342.48,
          "end": 344.013,
          "en": "and client components.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}